.TH "git-enhance" 1

.SH NAME
git-enhance - configure a checkout with the enhancements available for its repo

.SH SYNOPSIS
git enhance [--force]

.SH DESCRIPTION
Finds the enhancements that correspond to the current repo, writes the files
that enable them in the current worktree, and removes files it previously wrote
for enhancements that no longer apply. Running it again with nothing changed
does nothing, so it is safe to run at any time.

The repo name is the first path component under ~/repos of the main checkout,
found through the common git directory so that linked worktrees resolve to
their repo wherever they live. For example ~/repos/dart-sdk/sdk is
"dart-sdk". Checkouts outside of ~/repos have no enhancements, and bare
repositories are skipped.

.SH ENHANCEMENTS
.TP
Dev shells
If ~/repos/dotfiles/dev-shells/<repo>.nix exists, writes .envrc to use that
shell from the dotfiles flake with \fBuse flake\fR, and runs \fBdirenv allow\fR
on it. The file starts with \fBsource_up_if_exists\fR so an .envrc above the
checkout still loads. New files in dev-shells must be added to git before the
flake can see them.
.TP
Agent skills
If ~/.vibes/skills/repos/<repo> is a directory, adds an entry for it to
.agents/skills.json, using an absolute path. The file is edited semantically
and may contain other entries and keys, which are kept as they are. Entries
that point into ~/.vibes/skills/repos belong to git enhance: stale or duplicate
ones are removed, and the current one keeps its position if it is already
there. The file is only rewritten when its content changes, and is removed if
nothing but an empty entries list is left.

.SH OWNERSHIP
An .envrc written by git enhance starts with a "Generated by git-enhance"
comment, and is rewritten or removed freely, so don't edit it by hand. If an
.envrc without that comment exists when a dev shell applies, it is left alone
and the command exits non-zero. Move what the file does into git enhance, or
rerun with \fB--force\fR to replace it.

A skills.json that can't be parsed, or whose entries is not a list, is also
left alone with a non-zero exit unless \fB--force\fR is given.

Files tracked by the repo are never modified, even with \fB--force\fR.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
-f, --force
Replace an .envrc not written by git enhance, or a skills.json that is not
valid.

.SH ENVIRONMENT
GIT_ENHANCE_REPOS, GIT_ENHANCE_DOTFILES, and GIT_ENHANCE_SKILLS override the
~/repos, ~/repos/dotfiles, and ~/.vibes/skills/repos paths.
